+# Redis-backed Python echo API
+
+## Requirements coverage
+
+| Requirement | Evidence |
+| --- | --- |
+| REQ-001 | `app.echo_api.health()` returns `{'status': 'ok'}`. |
+| REQ-002 | `echo()` reads/writes a deterministic Redis cache key. |
+| REQ-003 | `app.redis_store.RedisCache` is the sole persistence adapter and speaks Redis RESP. |
+| REQ-004 | The modular backend is implemented in Python. |
+
+## Run
+
+Start a Redis server separately, then configure it without committing secrets:
+
+```sh
+export REDIS_URL='redis://:password@127.0.0.1:6379/0' # password is optional
+python -c "from app.echo_api import health, echo; print(health()); print(echo({'message': 'hello'}))"
+```
+
+`REDIS_URL` defaults to `redis://127.0.0.1:6379/0`. No third-party Python
+packages are required.
+
+## Test
+
+```sh
+python -m pytest -q
+```
